      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:4:52:3",
      "text": [
        " الرَّجُلِ يَؤُمُّ النِّسَاءَ لَيْسَ مَعَهُنَّ رَجُلٌ فِي الْفَرِيضَةِ قَالَ نَعَمْ وَ إِنْ كَانَ مَعَهُ صَبِيٌّ فَلْيَقُمْ إِلَى جَانِبِهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad, from Al Husayn, from Fazalat, from Hammad Bin Usman, from Ibrahim Bin Manmoun, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the man who led the women (in <span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>), there not being (another) man with them, in the Obligatory (<span class=\"iTxt\">Salāt</span>)’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘And even if there was a male child with him, so let him stand to his side’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ahmad ibn al-Husayn has narrated from Fadalah from Hammad ibn ‘Uthaman from Ibrahim ibn Maymun who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about a man who leads women in obligatory Salah (prayer) where there are no other men. He (the Imam) said, ‘Yes, he can do so and if there is a child he stands up on his side.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
